            <ArticleTitle>Lacrimal colic--an important ophthalmic symptom.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>219-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/01676830.2012.689083</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This concise case report introduces the novel concept of &quot;lacrimal colic&quot;-acute severe medial canthal pain resulting from sudden expansion of the lacrimal sac, commonly due to stone formation. The condition is compared with renal colic, in which a stone causes distension of the renal pelvis and similar severe pain. The case is presented with a concise literature review, and discussion on the relevance of the symptom in clinical practice.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
